{"kind":"request","text":"claude: refiling the docset speed-up with its sequencing corrected. This replaces eea00d2a, which I am retiring beside this filing. Substance unchanged.\n\nWHY REFILED. eea00d2a said \"sequenced last, behind ba9326ae, the statusview lane and the decision-records repairs\". ba9326ae is cancelled and retired — I retired it myself — so the first named gate does not exist. The decision-records gate is real and I have kept it. I originally recorded this as an assert on the row and left the conditions saying \"wait\"; hugh pointed out that a procedural snafu never implies the task should not be completed, and he is right. A request whose conditions still say to wait, with a correction filed alongside, makes the next reader reconcile two documents. This one says what is true in one place.\n\nWHAT IS STILL GENUINELY AHEAD OF IT. Only the decision-records repairs: d14e96fb and ae0d3d86 are both reported with ratified changes-requested verdicts, and the repair head is with me under 703ca542. That is one gate, not three, and when it clears this is next rather than last.\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH DOING, since it has sat a while. Hugh measured our CI and ranked this third of three opportunities — the one with the most headroom and the least certainty. That is exactly why the conditions ask for measurement rather than a claimed factor. internal/docset currently pays, per governing act, for signing, a repository copy, a reopen, an append and a snapshot, in order to observe projection semantics that workroom.Fold can answer from records in memory.\n\nTHE CONDITION I CARE MOST ABOUT IS (3), and it is not the speed. TestGateNoPageIsUnableToFlare must still fail when the flare rule is broken at its decision site. A suite that got faster by no longer reaching the thing it was written to catch is worse than the slow one, and it would pass every gate we have while being worse. Break it, watch that named assertion fail, revert, show the hashes.\n\nAND (2), because I have now been bitten by it twice today. Do not inherit any figure from this request. My 70.4 second uncached measurement is hours old, and when I checked the advisory-citation baseline in the neighbouring lane it was wrong by a wide margin and in units nobody could reconstruct. Measure at your own head, state the machine conditions, and let the numbers in this request be superseded by yours rather than reconciled with them.","body":{"conditions":"Replaces eea00d2a, whose sequencing clause named a retired gate; substance unchanged. SEQUENCING: behind your decision-records repair lanes only — d14e96fb and ae0d3d86 are still reported with ratified changes-requested verdicts, and the repair head is with planner under 703ca542. No other gate. Make internal/docset test projection semantics through workroom.Fold on in-memory records rather than through a Git-backed workspace, keeping one small Git-backed integration case to prove the adapter wiring is real. The behaviour under test is projection semantics, and the current shape pays for signing, a repository copy per governing act, a reopen, an append and a snapshot to observe it. (1) Measure before and after and report both figures from runs you actually performed: state the package wall time at the head you cut from and at the delivered head, each from a -count=1 run, and name the machine conditions. Load has produced figures varying by more than 3x on this machine today. (2) Do not quote a speedup factor you did not measure, and do not inherit any number from this request — treat every figure here as a reading someone took once. My own 70.4s uncached measurement is from earlier today and the neighbouring citation baseline turned out badly stale when checked. (3) Coverage must not narrow: every behaviour the current tests pin must still be pinned. TestGateNoPageIsUnableToFlare in particular must still fail when the flare rule is broken — prove it by breaking that rule at its decision site, watching that named assertion fail, and reverting; confirm identical file hashes afterwards. A faster suite that no longer catches the defect is a regression sold as an improvement. (4) Keep at least one case exercising the real Git-backed path end to end, so a fault in the adapter between records and workspace cannot pass unnoticed. (5) If some case genuinely cannot be expressed against workroom.Fold, leave it Git-backed and say which and why in the artifact rather than dropping it. (6) Exact clean pushed head, per-path artifacts resting on your promise plus current bases. (7) Gates green at the exact head with -count=1: gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check, go test ./... -count=1. (8) Independent review recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}